- No. No. Not you.


01:39:56.730 --> 01:39:58.515
Here. Drink some water. Come on.


01:39:58.689 --> 01:40:00.430
What's happening? You can't breathe?


01:40:00.604 --> 01:40:01.779
Drink some water. Come on.


01:40:06.218 --> 01:40:07.785
What is it? Are you having
a panic attack right now?


01:40:10.092 --> 01:40:12.007
You need to breathe. You're not
breathing properly. Come here.


01:40:15.314 --> 01:40:16.707
Hey, hey, it's all right.


01:40:22.365 --> 01:40:25.977
Hey, hey, hey. Hey. No, no, no.


01:40:33.898 --> 01:40:35.030
I'm really sorry.


01:40:40.557 --> 01:40:41.471
Okay, I'm really sorry.


01:40:59.880 --> 01:41:01.926
It is such a huge honor


01:41:02.100 --> 01:41:04.929
to have been guided by
a woman like Romy Mathis.


01:41:06.148 --> 01:41:09.890
She understands the importance
of being a voice for your peers


01:41:10.195 --> 01:41:12.241
and an advocate for
women around the world


01:41:12.415 --> 01:41:16.767
who might not have the same
opportunities that us, sitting here, have.


01:41:17.159 --> 01:41:21.511
So to be lifted up by a hero like her


01:41:21.685 --> 01:41:24.079
makes this experience
so much more exceptional.


01:41:26.516 --> 01:41:29.388
Who are we, as women?


01:41:30.085 --> 01:41:33.131
Modern leaders aren't
afraid to take chances


01:41:33.305 --> 01:41:36.700
embrace change, and usher
a team into the unknown.


01:41:37.135 --> 01:41:41.008
Sincerity, vulnerability,
and radical self-honesty


01:41:41.183 --> 01:41:44.621
will create a work environment
of shared learning, compassion,


01:41:44.795 --> 01:41:46.666
and true connection.


01:41:46.840 --> 01:41:48.842
Now, how do we do that?


01:41:49.278 --> 01:41:52.150
By making changes from top
to bottom to support women


01:41:52.324 --> 01:41:54.674
at every level across the company.


01:41:56.589 --> 01:41:58.635
If we dare to let go of expectations


01:41:58.809 --> 01:42:01.290
and move towards what scares us,


01:42:01.464 --> 01:42:03.596
we can often find unexpected strengths.


01:42:04.380 --> 01:42:07.557
Today, we celebrate genuine authenticity


01:42:07.731 --> 01:42:11.256
and true uniqueness in every
individual that works at Tensile.


01:42:12.127 --> 01:42:16.000
We invite each other to show
the world who we really are


01:42:16.174 --> 01:42:19.830
regardless of people's
assumptions and without fear.


01:42:44.724 --> 01:42:46.422
Oh, hey.


01:42:48.337 --> 01:42:49.425
You okay?


01:42:51.601 --> 01:42:53.124
You look like Grandma.


01:42:57.650 --> 01:42:58.956
How did you get here?


01:43:00.218 --> 01:43:01.306
I got a car.


01:43:01.959 --> 01:43:03.003
You did?


01:43:03.961 --> 01:43:05.484
That's expensive.


01:43:07.356 --> 01:43:08.444
Mom...


01:43:09.706 --> 01:43:11.273
...you have to come home.


01:43:13.318 --> 01:43:14.624
Dad needs you.


01:43:17.453 --> 01:43:19.498
He won't leave the theatre.


01:43:20.456 --> 01:43:23.676
He won't eat, and
he's reading the Bible.


01:43:25.765 --> 01:43:27.593
He'll forgive you, Mom.


01:43:27.767 --> 01:43:29.029
What did he tell you?


01:43:30.030 --> 01:43:31.031
Nothing.


01:43:33.251 --> 01:43:34.861
Mary forgave me.


01:43:42.434 --> 01:43:44.044
It's okay, Mom.


01:43:47.091 --> 01:43:48.310
It's okay.


01:43:52.314 --> 01:43:53.184
God.


01:43:54.316 --> 01:43:55.447
Okay.


01:44:02.846 --> 01:44:04.282
Please come home.


01:44:29.829 --> 01:44:31.178
It's all my fault.


01:44:33.050 --> 01:44:36.271
I told you that I was
someone else and I got angry


01:44:36.445 --> 01:44:38.838
because you didn't
know who I really was.


01:44:39.361 --> 01:44:43.930
And I'm so sorry. It's my
problem. It's my problem.


01:44:45.105 --> 01:44:49.371
Hey. What a great way
to start the year, huh?


01:44:52.025 --> 01:44:53.288
Um...


01:44:55.551 --> 01:44:57.161
Whatever happened to that intern?


01:44:57.335 --> 01:44:59.946
The one who bought me the coffee?


01:45:00.512 --> 01:45:03.602
I heard he took a job
at Kawasaki? In Tokyo?


01:45:07.432 --> 01:45:08.738
Good for him.


01:45:08.912 --> 01:45:10.087
Good for you, too.


01:45:12.698 --> 01:45:15.092
You didn't have anything
to do with that, did you?


01:45:17.486 --> 01:45:19.705
Why don't you come over
next week for drinks?


01:45:19.879 --> 01:45:21.794
I've got the house to myself.


01:45:23.013 --> 01:45:24.319
We can talk about it.


01:45:30.542 --> 01:45:32.457
Why don't you fuck off, Sebastian?


01:45:32.631 --> 01:45:34.764
Hey, careful, Romy.


01:45:34.938 --> 01:45:38.942
I'm not afraid of you, whatever
the fuck you're capable of.


01:45:39.116 --> 01:45:41.988
Of what you know, of what you
don't know. I don't give a shit.


01:45:42.467 --> 01:45:46.253
Just don't ever talk
to me like that again.


01:45:46.950 --> 01:45:50.388
If I want to be humiliated,
I'm gonna pay someone to do it.


01:45:53.609 --> 01:45:55.567
Now get the fuck out of my office.


01:46:07.579 --> 01:46:08.580
Five...


01:46:10.756 --> 01:46:11.670
four...


01:46:13.933 --> 01:46:15.152
three...


01:46:17.110 --> 01:46:18.198
two...


01:46:20.331 --> 01:46:21.376
one...

